From: airDroid <airdroid@airos.works>
Subject: [PATCH] virtio-gpu-virgl: poll fences every millisecond

QEMU looks for signalled virgl fences on a 10 ms timer. A guest frame is
done for Android when its fence signals, so every swap waited for the
next tick: 9.98 ms at the median between SwapBuffers and FrameCompleted in
Android's frame statistics, most of a 60 Hz frame, with the app short of
buffers behind it. Poll every millisecond while fences are pending.
---
--- a/hw/display/virtio-gpu-virgl.c
+++ b/hw/display/virtio-gpu-virgl.c
@@ -1116,7 +1116,14 @@
     virgl_renderer_poll();
     virtio_gpu_process_cmdq(g);
     if (!QTAILQ_EMPTY(&g->cmdq) || !QTAILQ_EMPTY(&g->fenceq)) {
-        timer_mod(gl->fence_poll, qemu_clock_get_ms(QEMU_CLOCK_VIRTUAL) + 10);
+        /*
+         * airDroid: every millisecond while fences are pending, not every
+         * ten. A guest frame is finished for Android when its fence
+         * signals: at 10 ms every swap waited for the next tick (9.98 ms at
+         * the median in Android's frame statistics), which is most of a
+         * 60 Hz frame and left apps waiting for a free buffer.
+         */
+        timer_mod(gl->fence_poll, qemu_clock_get_ms(QEMU_CLOCK_VIRTUAL) + 1);
     }
 }
 
